{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Make for yourself.</b> That they would sound before you like a king, as it is said: ״וַיְהִי בִישֻׁרוּן מֶלֶךְ״." "<b>Make for yourself.</b> From your own." "<b>Make for yourself.</b> You make them and use them, and no one else." "<b>For assembling the assembly.</b> When you wish to speak with the Sanhedrin and the rest of the people and to call them to gather to you, you call them by means of trumpets." "<b>And for journeying the camps.</b> At the time of setting out on journeys you sound them as a signal. Thus you find that they would journey by three — by the word of the Holy One, blessed be He, by the word of Moses, and by the trumpets (Beraita of Midrash ha-Torah, chapter 13)." "<b>Of beaten work.</b> From the existing material you shall make it — by hammering with the hammer."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The quotation is from Deuteronomy 33:5.", 4 "Rashi cites the Beraita of the 32 (Middot) or 49 rules of hermeneutics, commonly called Beraita de-Melechet ha-Mishkan; the exact referent here (פי״ג = chapter 13) is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:12.858177134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}